From: AgentBox
Subject: [PATCH] venus: no query feedback on a renderer without dma-buf

On a macOS host (krunkit, MoltenVK), feedback for the timestamp queries
ANGLE records around a three.js frame never reaches the feedback buffer
(a frame that only clears is fine), so vkGetQueryPoolResults with
VK_QUERY_RESULT_WAIT_BIT spins until Chromium's GPU watchdog kills the process and WebGL loses
its context (EXT_disjoint_timer_query). Without dma-buf, queries are
answered by the renderer, as with VN_PERF=no_query_feedback. Its debug
message is how AgentBox tells a driver with this fix (venus-chromium.sh).

---
diff --git a/src/virtio/vulkan/vn_command_buffer.c b/src/virtio/vulkan/vn_command_buffer.c
--- a/src/virtio/vulkan/vn_command_buffer.c
+++ b/src/virtio/vulkan/vn_command_buffer.c
@@ -1805,6 +1805,19 @@
    if (unlikely(VN_PERF(NO_QUERY_FEEDBACK)))
       return;
 
+   /* Without dma-buf (a macOS host), query feedback can fail to land and
+    * vkGetQueryPoolResults with WAIT then spins forever: the renderer
+    * answers instead. AgentBox finds this message in the driver to tell
+    * one with this fix.
+    */
+   if (!cmd->pool->device->physical_device->base.base.supported_extensions
+           .EXT_external_memory_dma_buf) {
+      if (VN_DEBUG(INIT))
+         vn_log(cmd->pool->device->instance,
+                "query feedback off: the renderer has no dma-buf");
+      return;
+   }
+
    if (unlikely(!query_pool->fb_buf)) {
       if (vn_query_feedback_buffer_init_once(cmd->pool->device, query_pool) !=
           VK_SUCCESS) {
